Deliberate. This library is installed with pip, not built by colcon.

colcon's ament_python build type (Humble) runs `setup.py --dry-run` and then
ast.literal_eval's the dumped metadata. This package is defined by
pyproject.toml, whose [project] table puts a SpecifierSet object and the whole
README into that dump, and neither is valid Python literal syntax, so the
build fails with a SyntaxError before it compiles a single module.

Making it a colcon package would mean moving the metadata back out of
pyproject.toml into a setup.py, which downgrades the library's packaging for
every other consumer of it. Installing it with pip is one line and is what
docker/Dockerfile already does.

Without this file colcon fails the whole workspace build. With it, colcon
builds perception_suite and leaves this alone. See ../README.md.
